          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What kind of activity is described for someone with COPD who gets breathless walking?",
          "answer": "The guidance I could retrieve does not describe specific activity plans for COPD. It does not name pacing, graded walking, or a set routine. It also does not give details of pulmonary rehabilitation.\n\nWhat the COPD activity note (*Staying active with COPD: breathing technique, pacing and the deconditioning spiral*) does say is that breathlessness on exertion often leads people to avoid activity. Muscles then weaken, so the same task feels harder, and breathlessness comes sooner. The note treats exercise as a therapy for this cycle, not just general advice. It also says that pulmonary rehabilitation is covered in a separate COPD guideline, but the passage I received did not include that section.\n\nPlease ask your clinician or respiratory team about:\n- Which types of walking or exercise suit you, and how much to start with.\n- Whether a structured programme such as pulmonary rehabilitation is appropriate for you.\n- How to pace activity and when to slow down or stop.\n\nSeek urgent care if breathlessness is severe, comes on suddenly, or comes with chest pain, confusion, or blue lips.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
          "risk_level": "routine",
